integ5 0070 = patches/pdl5/0068-glm-pdl-hc-chain.patch (overnight 2026-10-31), renumbered for the integrated stack on 3f94715d.
integ5 resolution: cuda_forward.zig Forward.set() and cuda_glue.zig Set keep attn5 0067's `dsel` beside this patch's `pdl_hc` (one initializer, one struct line).

pdl5 0068: a decode window's hc_post, hc_partial8 and hc_finish launch as dependents (TF_GLM_PDL_CHAIN's hc).
- glm_triton.cuh: pdl_wait / pdl_trigger (griddepcontrol, sm_90+; the glue builds native sm_120 SASS only).
- hc_post: wait first (every input is an earlier grid's), then trigger. hc_partial8: its 3 fn rows (immutable weights)
  load before the wait, x and part after; then trigger. hc_finish(_f32w): the norm weight, base and scale (immutable)
  load before the wait; x, the partials and every store after it; then trigger. No exit precedes any wait.
- cuda_glue.zig: Set.pdl_hc; hc_partial8, hc_finish and hc_post launch with it (decode rows only; the prompt kernel
  tf_glm_hc_partial has no wait and never does). cuda_forward.zig: Forward.set() sets it for decode windows only.
Needs 0067 (Chain). Exact by construction.

